# Shell scripts execute inside WSL and on the board. A CRLF in one is not
# an untidiness issue: it becomes part of the shebang and of every line
# continuation, so the script fails with "bad interpreter" or a syntax
# error at the first backslash.
#
# Other file types in this tree also carry CRLF (Yocto recipes, kas YAML,
# CMakeLists). They tolerate it, and normalising them is a separate change
# with a much larger diff - deliberately not done here.
*.sh text eol=lf
